<title>UK: Nigeria raises June crude prices by 25-41 cts.</title>
<headline>Nigeria raises June crude prices by 25-41 cts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigerian National Petroleum Corp (NNPC) raised crude contract formula prices for June by 27-41 cents a barrel, traders said.</p>
<p>Following are new prices for June versus benchmark Dated Brent</p>
<p>		    June	  May	  change</p>
<p>Bonny Light    +42 cts     +15 cts   up 17 cts</p>
<p>Qua Iboe	 +42 cts     +15 cts   up 17 cts</p>
<p>Forcados	 +11 cts     -30 cts   up 41 cts</p>
<p>Escravos	 +34 cts     +7 cts    up 27 cts</p>
<p>Brass River    +50 cts     +25 cts   up 25 cts</p>
<p>Pennington     +75 cts     +35 cts   up 40 cts</p>
<p>Bonny Medium   +1 ct	 -40 cts   up 41 cts</p>
<p>NNPC left unchanged its option to price crude five days ahead of bill of lading at plus five cents.</p>
<p>An option for deferred pricing 14 days after bill of lading was left unchanged at five cents a barrel.</p>
<p>-- Richard Mably, London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
